{number: 44}
{title: There Is a Fountain}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] There is a fountain filled with blood
Drawn from Immanuel's [G7] veins;
And [C] sinners plunged beneath that [F] flood
Lose [C] all their [G7] guilty [C] stains.
Lose all their guilty stains,
Lose [G7] all their guilty stains;
And [C] sinners plunged beneath that [F] flood
Lose [C] all their [G7] guilty [C] stains.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
The [C] dying thief rejoiced to see
That fountain in his [G7] day;
And [C] there may I, though vile as [F] he,
Wash [C] all my [G7] sins a-[C] way.
Wash all my sins away,
Wash [G7] all my sins away;
And [C] there may I, though vile as [F] he,
Wash [C] all my [G7] sins a-[C] way.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Dear [C] dying Lamb, Thy precious blood
Shall never lose its [G7] power
Till [C] all the ransomed church of [F] God
Be [C] saved, to [G7] sin no [C] more.
Be saved, to sin no more,
Be [G7] saved, to sin no more;
Till [C] all the ransomed church of [F] God
Be [C] saved, to [G7] sin no [C] more.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
E'er [C] since, by faith, I saw the stream
Thy flowing wounds sup-[G7] ply,
Re-[C] deeming love has been my [F] theme,
And [C] shall be [G7] till I [C] die.
And shall be till I die,
And [G7] shall be till I die;
Re-[C] deeming love has been my [F] theme,
And [C] shall be [G7] till I [C] die.
{end_of_verse}
